I arrive at the Ernakulam market.
It is morning now.
But it is very warm.
There is a small shop in front of the market.
I walk near that shop.
I need some water.
The shopkeeper is standing there.
"Please give me a bottle of water," I say.
The shopkeeper gives me the water.
"How much is it?" I ask.
"Twenty rupees," the shopkeeper says.
I open my bag.
I take money from it.
I give a twenty-rupee note.
He takes the money.
I drink a little water.
Now it is very refreshing.
Then I go inside the market.
